; The relief valve must be able to see a popped array query as dead.
;
; A read's index-binding equation is emitted when its registry row is
; created. The transformer used to re-emit an anchor for EVERY row in the
; table on every transform, so once the driver seeded its session-long
; registry, each conjunct's root implied the whole accumulated registry --
; and every check's live AIG cone therefore contained every read ever seen.
; The valve compares live mass against retained mass, so it concluded that
; nothing was reclaimable and never fired, however much popped content piled
; up: this file rebuilt zero times before the fix and twice after, running
; 1.5x faster on 42% of the memory at eight hundred queries.
;
; The tiny re-encode limit forces the valve into range; the point is that it
; fires at all, not how often.
; RUN: %solver --incremental -s --incremental-reencode-limit 2000 %s 2>&1 | %OutputCheck %s
; RUN: %solver --incremental-auto-engage-at 1 -s --incremental-reencode-limit 2000 %s 2>&1 | %OutputCheck %s
